WEBVTT

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:19.290
A light so bright that it can't be hidden
Breaks the silence and resurrects in this world

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:30.040
The dry land quakes violently
Sparks clash as we risk our lives

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.780
Let a miracle occur, just one more time

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:44.950
The power to regain the pages of memories I lost long ago

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:53.020
The trusting heart pierces the darkness
Search for the place where the soul rests

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:59.200
The sharp glint in my unblinking eye burns

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:06.700
Two souls - light and shadow
To the future shown in the crystal

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:13.310
Now moving  Overflowing in red  eyes

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:22.810
Silent Swordsman LV5 attacks Obelisk the Tormentor!

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:24.730
Not good enough, partner!

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.310
I activate my trap!

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.580
Mirror Force!

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:42.530
Too bad, partner.  You couldn't figure out my set card.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:45.980
No, I knew what your set card was.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:53.000
By activating Mirror Force, you completed my combo to defeat the Gods!

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.710
The three Gods will now vanish!

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:03.720
Strong Heart  Kind Heart

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:06.220
What?  Impossible!

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.190
He has a combo to defeat the Gods?

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:14.960
The Gods' attack points have decreased, but Yugi has no monsters on his field.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:20.700
Partner!

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.200
Here I go, my other self!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.210
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Magnet Reverse from my hand!

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:36.530
If a Rock or Machine was sent to the graveyard this turn, I Special Summon it faceup in defense position!

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.060
Valkyrion the Magna Warrior resurrects!

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:45.030
This Special Summon activates Slifer’s Lightning Bullet!

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:56.660
But due to my trap Magnet Force, Lightning Bullet is deflected to your monster!

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:02.410
Obelisk!

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.530
Then I activate Valkyrion the Magna Warrior’s effect!

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:09.250
Separate into Magnet Warriors!

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.250
It divided into three!

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:18.700
Slifer’s Lightning Bullet will automatically fire on the newly-summoned monsters.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:31.370
Magnet Force’s effect sends all Lightning Bullets back to your monsters!

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.320
Wow.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.220
He defeated the three Gods?

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.960
Unbelievable!

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.890
Yugi defeated the three Gods…

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.330
...at once!

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.730
He really did perform a miracle!

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.730
That was incredible!

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.230
You did it, Yugi!

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.730
That’s my grandson!

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:08.740
My other self, I learned something by battling together with you.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:15.010
If someone has great power, that power is his greatest weakness.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:18.040
Use the Gods' power to defeat the Gods.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:25.360
When I watched you use the Gods in battle...

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.370
...I subconsciously thought of ways to defeat them.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.030
As you should, partner.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:38.380
A true duelist instinctively wants to fight against the strongest.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.010
And that's also true with me.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:44.510
I haven’t unleashed all my power yet!

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:49.750
I’ll unleash all my power too, my other self!

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:52.390
Right!  Here I go, partner!

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.490
My turn!  I draw!

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:58.760
I activate the spell card, Polymerization from my hand!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.090
I tribute Gazelle the King of Mythical Beasts and Berfomet from my hand...

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:07.410
...to summon Chimera the Flying Mythical Beast!

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.410
Wow.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:15.740
He just lost his Gods, but he already has another powerful monster.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:19.980
Go, Chimera!  Attack Alpha the Magnet Warrior!

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.690
Impact Dash!

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.790
I end my turn.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.410
He's strong!

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:39.800
Yugi finally defeated the Gods, but Atem still has the advantage.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.710
You’re wrong.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:42.790
Big brother?

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:50.150
Yugi has lower life points, but he's the first to defeat the three Gods with his combo.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:52.670
Things are going his way.

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:57.320
Yugi, I now believe what you said!

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.320
Kaiba!

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:03.970
Kaiba is cheering for Yugi?

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.470
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:13.470
I tribute Beta and Gamma the Magnet Warriors to summon Buster Blader!

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.570
Come out, Buster Blader!

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:22.480
Yugi isn't backing down.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:26.350
He summoned a high-class monster in just one turn!

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:28.180
He’s incredible.

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:32.680
For them, it doesn’t matter if the Gods are in play or not.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.950
Here I go, my other self!

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:39.110
Buster Blader attacks!  Destruction Sword!

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:41.730
Slice up Chimera!

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.150
Not bad, partner.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:07:00.520
But when Chimera is destroyed, its effect activates!

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:06.050
I can Special Summon either Berfomet or Gazelle from my graveyard!

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:09.530
I Special Summon Berfomet!

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.530
Resurrect, Berfomet!

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.130
Impressive!

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.530
Atem keeps bringing out monsters!

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:19.540
But since the Gods are gone...

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:26.540
...Atem doesn't have many monsters in his deck that have more attack points than Buster Blader.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:29.550
That means Yugi has the advantage.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.810
I end my turn.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:36.810
Partner, you summoned some powerful monsters.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:37.850
But…

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:40.560
It's my turn!  I draw!

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.090
I tribute Berfomet!

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:45.560
Come out, Archfiend of Gilfer!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:53.060
I set one card and end my turn.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:54.890
Archfiend of Gilfer?

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:58.330
It has lower attack points than Buster Blader.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:05.580
But when it's destroyed, it lowers the opposing monster’s attack points by 500.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:10.130
I know that’s what my other self is going for.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:13.930
But this is my first chance to attack.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:16.190
I can’t just stay put!

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:18.250
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.750
I set a card.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.100
Then Buster Blader attacks Archfiend of Gilfer!

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:27.340
Go, Buster Blader!

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.610
Dragon Sword!

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:39.480
Archfiend of Gilfer’s effect now activates!

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:43.750
When it's sent to the graveyard, it turns into an Equip Spell.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:47.430
The equipped monster loses 500 attack points!

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:54.310
I end my turn.

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:56.360
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.290
I set one card.

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:02.640
I activate the spell card, Awakening from Beyond from my hand.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:07.210
You get to draw two cards from your deck.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:12.480
In exchange, I can add a monster card in my graveyard to my hand.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:16.040
Partner, draw two cards.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:22.320
I add a monster card in my graveyard to my hand.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:23.930
Which card is it...

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:33.130
Other than the Gods, The Tricky is the monster with the most attack points in his graveyard.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.670
The Tricky is a Level 5 monster.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:40.680
He needs to discard a card to Special Summon it.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:48.440
But since that's the one card in his hand, he has no other cards to pay the cost.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:55.320
So he must be bringing back a monster with lower attack points than Buster Blader.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:59.150
Partner, I can anticipate what you're thinking.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:04.700
But I'm a step or two ahead of you in this duel!

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:09.330
This is the monster I’ll resurrect from my graveyard!

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.570
Come out!

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:13.070
Swift Gaia the Fierce Knight!

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.310
What?  Gaia?

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:28.220
When it's the only card in my hand, I can summon Swift Gaia the Fierce Knight without tributing!

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:31.960
No way!  How did Gaia end up in your graveyard?

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:36.960
There was one opportunity to send Gaia to the graveyard.

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:40.360
I'll go first.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.740
I draw!

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:43.830
I discard one card.

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:50.910
That was your chance to send Gaia to the graveyard.

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:55.750
The first card you discarded was Swift Gaia the Fierce Knight!

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:58.370
That's right, partner.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:01.890
I anticipated this scenario from the start.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.910
From the start?

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:10.770
Yes.  There are powerful cards that only I can control because I'm the Pharaoh.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.770
Such as the three Gods.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:17.970
They do give me a huge advantage.

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:21.410
But in the event that they're defeated...

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:26.910
Partner, I knew you had the potential to defeat the Gods!

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:33.650
He anticipated from the start that Yugi would defeat the Gods?

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:38.800
For a true duelist, power is just a ruse.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:42.800
The true battle begins when the Gods are gone.

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:51.670
The extreme tension, miraculous draws and faith in our cards have led to this ultimate battle!

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:53.320
Here I go, partner!

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:57.820
Swift Gaia the Fierce Knight attacks Buster Blader!

00:11:58.690 --> 00:11:59.820
Yugi!

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:06.160
You have the power to repel the Pharaoh’s fighting spirit.

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:10.170
The one who can let the Pharaoh sleep in peace forever...

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:13.830
And return him to his friends from 3000 years ago…

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:16.830
...is you.  And you alone.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:18.930
Spiral Shaver!

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.970
Spiral Shaver!

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.180
Yugi!

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:51.170
I activate my trap card, Soul Rope!

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:55.960
When my monster is destroyed and sent to the graveyard...

00:12:55.960 --> 00:13:03.180
...I can pay 1000 life points to Special Summon a Level 4 monster from my deck!

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:08.930
I Special Summon Witch of the Black Forest from my deck in defense position!

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:14.190
I end my turn.

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:17.900
Atem has a big advantage again.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:21.510
2300 attack points is huge at this point.

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:22.840
Yeah.

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:26.020
Atem made better predictions.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.400
Not necessarily.

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:33.520
Why did Yugi pay 1000 life points to have a monster on his field?

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:36.210
I see!  So he can tribute it!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.950
That’s right.  Yugi hasn’t given up!

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:40.340
Yugi!

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:41.420
My turn!

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:42.920
I draw!

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.940
I tribute Witch of the Black Forest!

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.160
Come here, Summoned Skull!

00:13:53.220 --> 00:14:00.210
Due to Witch of the Black Forest, I get a monster with 1500 or lower defense points from my deck.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.940
I add Marshmallon to my hand!

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:06.450
Summoned Skull?

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:10.040
Gaia the Fierce Knight and Summoned Skull.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:14.190
They're both monsters that supported and battled alongside Yugi.

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:20.270
Yeah.  They're monsters that saved both Yugis from tight spots.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:26.610
But now these allies have to fight as enemies.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:33.610
The ones who are suffering most in this duel might be the monsters.

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:36.040
Here I go, my other self!

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.230
Summoned Skull attacks!

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:39.540
Magic Lightning!

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:47.630
Destroy Gaia the Fierce Knight!

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:54.460
I end my turn!

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:56.640
Impressive, partner.

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:59.800
You quickly played a card to make a comeback.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:03.890
I’ve never felt this much fear in a duel before.

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:12.310
That’s because you were always behind me for support.

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:16.310
But now you're in front of me as my opponent.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:20.050
We’ve overcome challenges together.  And grew together.

00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:24.200
You’re my greatest rival, Yugi Muto!

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:27.470
There’s only one way to defeat you.

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:32.360
Believe in myself and my deck!

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:33.670
My turn!

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:37.680
Since you create miracles, I’ll create miracles too!

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:41.070
I'll summon Big Shield Gardna!

00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:41.910
I draw!

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:47.690
I summon Big Shield Gardna in defense position!

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:52.170
Huh?  What's going on?

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:56.270
Atem said the monster's name before he drew it.

00:15:56.270 --> 00:15:58.890
As if he knew which card he'd draw.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:02.700
No, he didn't know what card he would draw.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:06.400
The Pharaoh drew the card he envisioned.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.950
The card he envisioned?

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.050
That’s impossible!

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:14.640
The deck's card order is set at the start.

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:15.710
No.

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:21.720
I used to believe that a draw is determined by fate.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:27.910
But the Pharaoh is bending fate to his will.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:33.190
Bending fate to his will?

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:39.280
Atem and Yugi's duel is exceeding our imaginations.

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:41.570
I end my turn.

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:43.430
My turn!

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:46.750
I activate Pot of Greed!

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:50.350
I draw two cards from my deck.

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:54.250
Then I Special Summon Watapon!

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:59.760
I tribute Watapon to summon Curse of Dragon!

00:17:04.090 --> 00:17:08.290
Yugi summoned another high-class monster!

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.650
Go, Summoned Skull!

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:12.290
Magic Lightning!

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:16.310
Why is he attacking when Big Shield Gardna has higher defense points?

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:21.200
This is fine!

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:34.790
When this monster is attacked, it switches to attack position.

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:37.760
And it only has 100 attack points.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:42.400
Curse of Dragon attacks Big Shield Gardna!

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:44.210
Dragon Flame!

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:54.810
I end my turn.

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:59.230
Now Atem and Yugi’s life points are about equal!

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:03.410
And Yugi has two high-class monsters on his field.

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:05.820
I can see Yugi winning!

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:11.490
What's wrong, Anzu?

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:13.830
I can’t watch anymore.

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:17.840
I don’t think Atem wants to leave.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:23.570
I know he wants to stay with us.  So why?

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:28.850
Anzu, they're no longer battling with their own free will.

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:32.690
They're battling due to the duelists' souls ingrained into their decks.

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:34.810
Duelists' souls?

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:40.290
They battled many duelists to reach this point.

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:46.830
Me, Kaiba, Marik, Bakura, Mai, Haga, Kajiki, Pegasus...

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:53.870
Their souls - along with many other duelists they faced - honed their decks.

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:58.140
So a duelist must also fight for them.

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:00.390
Jonouchi…

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:06.080
Returning to the afterlife - they're not thinking about that anymore.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:10.080
No one can stop this duel anymore.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:15.230
As duelists, their souls are pushing them to battle.

00:19:15.890 --> 00:19:19.420
Regardless of what fate awaits them.

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:23.180
There’s nothing we can do.

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:27.610
Even if it makes us sad, friendship is about seeing this through.

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:29.910
Right.

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:36.530
I can feel the pulse of the souls in my deck.

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:39.080
Thanks for waiting, Mahad!

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:40.690
Here I go, partner!

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:42.920
My turn!  I draw!

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:48.590
I activate the spell card, Dark Magic Curtain from my hand!

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:59.940
By paying half my life points, I can Special Summon Dark Magician from my deck!

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:11.240
Dark Magician!

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:14.980
It's their ace card.  The one both Yugis trust.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:17.220
This is when he summons it?

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:22.230
Then I activate the spell card on my field, Book of Secret Arts!

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:26.970
Dark Magician gains 300 attack and defense points!

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:32.460
Go, Dark Magician!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.970
Attack Summoned Skull!

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:37.240
Black Magic!

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:50.080
Mahad…

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:57.000
Pharaoh, after 3,000 years, I once again devote my soul to you!

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:00.350
What is it, sister?

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:03.330
I-It’s nothing.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:10.070
Why does Dark Magician make me feel nostalgic and heartbroken?

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:13.070
I knew Dark Magician would make an appearance.

00:21:13.070 --> 00:21:16.810
Partner, this is my final ace in the hole.

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:20.810
My most powerful servant, Dark Magician!

00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:25.820
You can't win unless you defeat Dark Magician!

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:32.030
I will defeat Dark Magician!

00:21:46.500 --> 00:22:01.130
Right now, we don't need a map

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:16.840
The miracle that tore through the darkness is in my hand

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:22.680
Without a goal in mind

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:31.260
We just step towards our dream

00:22:31.640 --> 00:22:36.900
EYE'S  As you sense it

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:45.370
Your eye will find it

00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:51.180
Oh! EYE'S  What you wish for

00:22:51.960 --> 00:22:59.320
Will touch your soul

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:02.570
In a duel

00:23:13.710 --> 00:23:19.310
I thought their duel will last forever, but it will soon end.

00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:22.110
That's when the other Yugi will...

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:28.260
Do you remember the ring of friendship we drew on our hands with a marker?

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:32.730
No matter how far apart we are, this ring unites us.

00:23:32.730 --> 00:23:35.350
No matter how far apart we are...

00:23:35.690 --> 00:23:39.500
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
The Story That Ends In Light

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:41.510
The duel comes to an end.
